<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfred Meyer-Waldeck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1864">1864</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfred Meyer-Waldeck was a German naval officer and the last governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiaozhou-bay">Kiautschou Bay</a> concession in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, from 1911. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, supported by British troops, attacked in 1914, he defended Tsingtao through the siege until he surrendered on 7 November 1914. He spent the rest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> as a prisoner in Japan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-meyer-waldeck.jpg" alt="Alfred Meyer-Waldeck" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfred_Meyer-Waldeck_(1911).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
